{
  "window_id": "w0012",
  "observed_failures": [
    {
      "filename": "034.jpg",
      "field": "date",
      "prediction": "2018-08-09",
      "symptom": "Date components appear transposed/misread; receipt shows '09/03/2018' which under DD/MM/YYYY is 2018-03-09, but output is 2018-08-09."
    },
    {
      "filename": "074.jpg",
      "field": "total_amount",
      "prediction": "702.00",
      "symptom": "OCR misreads the leading '1' of '102.00' as '7' on the 'Total incl. of GST' line; agent commits to this noisy read without cross-pass consensus. The receipt clearly shows Subtotal 102.00, Payment 102.00, Total Rounded 102.00."
    },
    {
      "filename": "077.jpg",
      "field": "total_amount",
      "prediction": "23.26",
      "symptom": "Receipt has 'Total (Inclusive of GST): 23.26', 'Rounding Adj: -0.01', and final 'TOTAL: 23.25'. Agent returns the pre-rounding inclusive total rather than the final post-rounding TOTAL line."
    },
    {
      "filename": "078.jpg",
      "field": "total_amount",
      "prediction": "\"\" (empty string)",
      "symptom": "Extraction failure path emits an empty string into the xlsx cell instead of a real null; receipt actually contains a legible 'Total RM 21.00' after discount/rounding so full extraction failure is itself a defect."
    }
  ],
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "id": "RC1-no-field-extraction-in-ocr-skill",
      "description": "The original image-ocr SKILL.md only documents generic image_to_string / image_to_data flows. It defines no keyword-priority logic, no exclusion keywords, no two-line fallback, and no numeric/date normalization for receipts. The task hint lists a very specific priority ladder (GRAND TOTAL > TOTAL RM/TOTAL: RM > TOTAL AMOUNT > TOTAL/AMOUNT/...) and an explicit exclusion list, none of which are codified anywhere in the skill set. The agent must reinvent all of this per run, which leads to inconsistent handling of 'Total (Inclusive of GST)' vs final rounded 'TOTAL:' lines (077) and to mistaking 'Total incl. of GBT 702.00' for the authoritative total (074)."
    },
    {
      "id": "RC2-single-pass-ocr-no-consensus",
      "description": "image-ocr documents a multi_pass_ocr pattern only at the full-text-concatenation level ('join all variants'), not at the field level. There is no guidance to run several PSMs/preprocessing variants and take a majority / plausibility-filtered vote on the extracted amount or date. For a receipt like 074 where one pass yields 702.00 and multiple other sources on the same receipt (Subtotal, Payment, Total Rounded) read 102.00, a per-field voting / sanity-check step would correct the misread."
    },
    {
      "id": "RC3-no-date-locale-guidance",
      "description": "No skill specifies how to disambiguate DD/MM/YYYY vs MM/DD/YYYY for receipts (which are Malaysian in this corpus and use DD/MM). There is also no rule to prefer the date nearest the 'Date:' / 'Invoice' label, no OCR-digit sanity filter (e.g. month > 12 implies the other interpretation), and no rule to reject obviously corrupted dates in favor of a secondary candidate elsewhere on the receipt. This causes 034's date to come out transposed."
    },
    {
      "id": "RC4-xlsx-schema-failure-path-underspecified",
      "description": "The original xlsx SKILL.md focuses on financial-model color coding, formula hygiene, and recalc; it does not describe the 'strict-schema, graded-line-by-line' output contract this task uses. In particular it does not say: write Python None (never ''/'nan'/'None') on extraction failure, write amounts as strings with exactly two decimals, use a specific sheet name, use index=False, and verify by re-reading. The 078 cell holding '' (empty string) rather than a real null is a direct consequence."
    },
    {
      "id": "RC5-skill-coverage-gap-for-receipt-total-semantics",
      "description": "Even with keyword priority, the skills do not teach the semantic rule 'prefer the final rounded / post-adjustment TOTAL over an earlier Inclusive-GST line when both are present on the same receipt'. This is what breaks 077 (23.26 vs 23.25 after rounding -0.01). Related: there is no exclusion for lines like 'Total Item(s):', 'Total Savings', 'Total Gross', or 'Total Sales Incl GST' when a later strict 'TOTAL' line exists, so agent heuristics keep diverging across runs."
    },
    {
      "id": "RC6-no-cross-skill-handoff-for-hard-images",
      "description": "openai-vision is loaded but the skills do not describe when/how to invoke vision as a fallback when Tesseract confidence is low or when per-field voting disagrees. For borderline receipts (074, 078) a documented escalation path 'if Tesseract per-field confidence < threshold OR amount regex yields multiple incompatible candidates, call openai-vision with a strict JSON schema for date+total' would recover accuracy without changing the primary pipeline."
    }
  ],
  "skill_defects": [
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defects": [
        "No codified receipt field-extraction logic (priority tiers, exclusions, two-line fallback).",
        "Multi-pass OCR described only as text-concatenation, not as per-field voting/consensus.",
        "No date normalization helper (format detection, DD/MM vs MM/DD disambiguation, ISO output).",
        "No null-safe per-image pipeline that returns None on failure instead of empty strings.",
        "No deterministic filename-ordered batch iterator restricted to image extensions."
      ]
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "defects": [
        "No 'strict-schema output' section covering: exact sheet name, exact column order, index=False, lexicographic row order, string-typed numeric fields, real None (not '', 'nan', 'None'), and a round-trip verification step.",
        "Guidance privileges formulas-over-values, which is actively wrong for graders that compare literal cell contents.",
        "No warning about pandas default NaN leaking into cells as the string 'nan' under some readers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "skill": "openai-vision",
      "defects": [
        "No documented escalation protocol from Tesseract to vision for low-confidence receipt fields.",
        "No strict-JSON prompt template for extracting {date_iso, total_amount_two_decimals} with explicit null semantics."
      ]
    },
    {
      "skill": "pdf",
      "defects": [
        "Out of scope for this task; no changes required beyond leaving it unchanged."
      ]
    },
    {
      "skill": "video-frame-extraction",
      "defects": [
        "Out of scope for this task; no changes required beyond leaving it unchanged."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "repair_recommendations": [
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "changes": [
        "Add a 'Structured Field Extraction (Receipts/Forms)' section that defines ordered priority tiers (GRAND TOTAL > TOTAL:RM/TOTAL RM > TOTAL AMOUNT > NETT/NET TOTAL / TOTAL DUE / AMOUNT DUE / BALANCE DUE / bare TOTAL / bare AMOUNT) and an EXCLUSIONS list (SUBTOTAL, SUB TOTAL, TAX, GST, SST, DISCOUNT, CHANGE, CASH TENDERED) that is evaluated BEFORE tier matching.",
        "Specify a two-line fallback: if the matched keyword line has no numeric value, scan the next non-empty, non-excluded line and take its last number.",
        "Mandate output types: amount as str formatted via f\"{v:.2f}\" with commas and currency symbols stripped; date as ISO YYYY-MM-DD; None on any failure, never '' or 'nan'.",
        "Add a 'Per-Field Multi-Pass Consensus' subsection: run >=3 preprocess/PSM variants (gray+autocontrast PSM 6, inverted PSM 6, upscale+sharpen PSM 4; plus PSM 11 as recall booster); extract candidate amounts per variant; prefer a value that (a) appears in multiple variants and (b) is consistent with a Subtotal/Payment/Rounded cross-reference on the same receipt.",
        "Add a 'Final-Total-Over-Inclusive-GST' rule: when both 'Total (Inclusive of GST)' and a later strict 'TOTAL:' / 'Total Rounded' / 'Total After Rounding' line are present, prefer the later rounded line; add 'Total Item(s)', 'Total Qty', 'Total Savings', 'Total Gross' to exclusions.",
        "Add date handling: enumerate DD/MM/YYYY, DD-MM-YYYY, YYYY-MM-DD, YYYY/MM/DD, DD Mon YYYY, DD-Mon-YYYY, DD/MM/YY in that order; if a parse yields month>12, auto-swap day/month; prefer the match nearest a 'Date' / 'INVOICE' / 'TAX INVOICE' anchor and reject obviously corrupted dates (year outside 2000-2099) in favor of the next candidate.",
        "Add a null-safe per-image pipeline example (try/except, always returns {'date': ..., 'total_amount': ...}) and a deterministic iter_images(dir) helper that sorts by filename and filters hidden/non-image files."
      ]
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "changes": [
        "Add a top-level 'Strict-Schema Outputs (graded line-by-line)' section with a checklist: exact path, exact single sheet name, exact column names/order, index=False, lexicographic row sort, string dtype for formatted numeric fields, real None for missing, no extra sheets/columns.",
        "Document the canonical pandas pattern: build list[dict] -> DataFrame(columns=[...]) -> sort_values(stable) -> astype('object') on numeric-looking string columns -> ExcelWriter with explicit sheet_name='<task sheet>' and index=False.",
        "Add a 'Pitfalls' subsection enumerating: float 47.7 vs str '47.70' trailing-zero loss; NaN leaking as the literal string 'nan'; accidental Sheet1 from omitting sheet_name; thousand-separators/currency prefixes left in value; adding success/confidence debug columns that fail grading.",
        "Add a self-verification snippet that re-reads the file and asserts sheet list, column list, lexicographic order, and that non-null amount strings match N.NN with exactly two decimal places.",
        "Scope the existing 'use formulas, not hardcoded values' guidance explicitly to models/reports and note it does NOT apply to strict-schema extraction outputs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "skill": "openai-vision",
      "changes": [
        "Add an 'Escalation from Tesseract' subsection: when per-field consensus is empty or when candidates disagree, call GPT-4o with an exact JSON schema {\"date\":\"YYYY-MM-DD|null\",\"total_amount\":\"N.NN|null\"} and detail='high', then enforce the same formatting rules (two-decimal string, ISO date, real nulls).",
        "Provide a receipt-specific prompt template that instructs the model to honor the same keyword priority and exclusion list defined in image-ocr, so Tesseract and vision stages produce semantically comparable outputs for voting.",
        "Document a cost-guard: only escalate images where Tesseract confidence is low or consensus failed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "skill": "pdf",
      "changes": [
        "No change required for this task."
      ]
    },
    {
      "skill": "video-frame-extraction",
      "changes": [
        "No change required for this task."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "confidence": {
    "overall": 0.78,
    "notes": "High confidence on RC1, RC4, RC5 (directly supported by the four failing cells and visible OCR evidence in the window). Medium confidence on RC2/RC3 (plausible per-field voting and date-locale rules would fix 034/074 but the window only shows one Tesseract pass per image, so impact estimation is indirect). RC6 is a general robustness recommendation, not strictly required to pass the 4 failing cells."
  }
}
